                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly pretty solid. Introduces a lot of building blocks that come back (for better or worse) later in the series. This one really starts to establish a broader lore that isn't as connected to the first few games (at least not on first glance), and I found that to be fairly interesting. Shame they fumbled that concept pretty hard later on, but I won't hold that against this game. This game features some pretty decent voice acting, interesting and visually appealing locations, and decently solid work in guiding you from area to area.\n\nGenerally speaking, I would consider this game to be the last of the original quality of the series. It's not quite as good as the previous three games, but the difference isn't as noticeable between this game and the previous three as it is between this game and the next few games. Long live the Red Riding Hood Sisters, and I'm so sorry you became an obligatory thing to throw in to a lot of the later games.\n\nStill, the point remains. This game is great :)",
